[TEXT] ## Phase 2 → Phase 3

Both direct-IP probes return **100% loss** with **"Destination Net Unreachable"** from the respective gateways:
- `172.16.10.254` (Campus 1 gateway) has no route to `10.5.0.0/x`
- `10.5.0.254` (Campus 2 gateway) has no route to `172.16.0.0/x`

This is a **real routing symptom**. Active lead: routing failure between Campus 1 (172.16.x.x) and Campus 2 (10.5.x.x/10.6.x.x). The gateways themselves return ICMPs, so the fault lies in the routing control plane. This topology has multiple routers (router7, router8, router16, router17, etc.) — mapping to the OSPF/FRR fault family.
